## Doc map

**This table is the only place a doc path is written down.** `.claude/rules/*`,
`.claude/hooks/*`, skills and agents all defer to it. Keep prose docs to the
minimum the code cannot say for itself; everything else is read from the code,
via the `navigator` agent.

| Working on | Read (on demand) | Update when it breaks |
|---|---|---|
| {{a code surface, e.g. `backend/app/routers/**`}} | {{the generated reference, or "the router itself"}} | {{the regenerate command + the client mirror to move with it}} |
| {{another surface, e.g. `frontend/src/**`}} | {{the files themselves; name the route table}} | — |
| {{frontend **visual** work}} | {{the one visual-spec doc, if any}} | {{that doc, when a spec value changed}} |
| a product/domain question | the one relevant `##` section of {{product doc}}, never the whole file | — |
| a bug that could recur | `docs/backlogs/debug/` — search for a matching lesson before debugging | a lesson in `docs/backlogs/debug/` |

**Docs change only when something breaks a contract** — a response shape, a
schema or access-control decision, a visual spec value. Then the "Update when it
breaks" column above applies. A behaviour-preserving change updates nothing; the
Stop hook nudges and the escape marker is in the **`cook` skill** §10.

**Never a mandated read:** `docs/backlogs/goals/` is written only by
`scripts/goal` (a SessionStart hook injects the open one), and
`docs/backlogs/research/` is a write destination, not context to load.

**Generated, never hand-edited, never read whole:** {{list them, with the
command that regenerates each — and put the same paths in `GENERATED_FILES` in
`.claude/harness.conf`}}. Edit the source and regenerate. A "why" belongs beside
the code it explains.

If the area you touched has no row here, ask whether a doc update is needed —
don't silently skip, and don't invent a path outside this table.

